<title>GERMANY: Kohl on best-seller list with unification book.</title>
<headline>Kohl on best-seller list with unification book.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor Helmut Kohl has stormed on to Germany's bestseller lists with unification memoirs entitled &quot;I Wanted German Unity&quot;.</p>
<p>The book, penned by two tabloid journalists on the basis of interviews with Kohl, leapt into seventh place on the list of bestselling non-fiction books in Monday's news weekly Der Spiegel. Publishers Ullstein said it had sold 100,000 copies.</p>
<p>They said the rights had been sold for a number of foreign language editions and that there was interest from as far afield as Korea, India and China.</p>
</text>
